      "text": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the panda character Er Er from <Picture 1>, a white, round-bodied cartoon figure with black ears and limbs, pink cheeks, and no eyebrows. He appears in the background but does not interact or speak.\n<Subject 2> is the bear character Bu Bu from <Picture 2>, a brown, chubby cartoon bear with small ears, orange cheeks, simple dot eyes, and explicitly no eyebrows. He is the main focus of this shot.\n<Subject 3> is the forest scene environment from <Picture 3>, featuring soft green grass, dappled sunlight, colorful flowers, and a large red-and-white spotted mushroom (Amanita style) growing on the ground.\n<Audio 1> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 2> (S1). It provides the vocal quality for the dialogue.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] The target video features <Subject 2> in a close-up shot within <Subject 3>. <Subject 2> rubs his eyes sleepily, looks at a nearby mushroom with suspicion, and delivers a line of dialogue referencing <Audio 1> for timbre. <Subject 1> is visible in the periphery/background but remains passive. The art style is flat 2D animation.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved - The visual identity of the panda is retained; he serves as a static background element without movement or expression changes.\n<Subject 2>: fully_preserved - The visual identity of the bear is retained. His lack of eyebrows is strictly enforced.\n<Subject 3>: partially_preserved - The specific lighting and floral details are adapted to fit a close-up composition focusing on the bear and the mushroom.\n<Audio 1>: reference - The voice timbre guides the delivery of <Subject 2>'s lines without copying the original signal directly.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a flat 2D anime style with cel shading, clean lines, and vibrant colors consistent with the reference sheets.\n[Shot 1] At 00:00.000, the camera frames a close-up of <Subject 2>, the brown bear. The background shows blurred elements of <Subject 3>, including green grass and flowers, and a hint of <Subject 1> standing further back. The large spotted mushroom is positioned clearly in the foreground relative to the bear's gaze.\nAt 00:00.500, <Subject 2> raises a paw to rub his eye slowly, blinking heavily, displaying a sleepy demeanor.\nAt 00:02.500, he lowers his paw and tilts his head to the side, fixing his gaze on the mushroom with an expression shifting from drowsiness to suspicion. The camera performs a very slight push-in (zoom) to emphasize his facial change.\nAt 00:04.000, <Subject 2> speaks. Using the voice timbre referenced from <Audio 1>, he says in a slow, groggy tone: <d>[Chinese] 嗯……可是那个蘑菇……好像有毒？</d>. He pauses slightly before the word \"poison\" (有毒).\nAt 00:07.500, the shot holds on his suspicious face until the end. No music plays throughout the clip.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft ambient nature sounds, such as gentle wind and distant bird chirps, fill the silence between the dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
